TITLE:: UDef
summary:: Reusable pseudo-UGen definitions, callable like a real UGen.
categories:: UGens>Synthesis
related:: Classes/SynthDef, Reference/UGens

DESCRIPTION::

A UDef is a named, reusable sub-graph of UGens that you call just like a real
UGen. Define one once with an code::ar::, code::kr::, or code::ir:: function, then
call code::UDef(\name).ar(...):: anywhere inside a link::Classes/SynthDef:: to
splice that graph in. It is a lightweight alternative to link::Classes/SynthDef#*wrap::
for factoring out and sharing DSP building blocks.

UDef is a link::Classes/Singleton::, so code::UDef(\name):: always returns the
same registered instance for a given name -- defining and later fetching use the
same syntax.

code::
// define a pseudo-UGen named \saturate
UDef(\saturate, ar: { |in, amount = 4|
    (in * amount).tanh / amount.tanh
});

// use it like any UGen inside a SynthDef
(
SynthDef(\driven, { |out = 0, freq = 100|
    var sig = Saw.ar(freq);
    sig = UDef(\saturate).ar(sig, amount: 8);
    Out.ar(out, (sig * 0.2) ! 2)
}).add;
)
::

SUBSECTION:: Multiple rates

A single UDef can define more than one rate. Fetch-and-call picks the rate you ask
for:

code::
UDef(\ramp,
    ar: { |dur = 1| Line.ar(0, 1, dur) },
    kr: { |dur = 1| Line.kr(0, 1, dur) }
);

UDef(\ramp).ar(dur: 2);   // audio-rate Line
UDef(\ramp).kr(dur: 2);   // control-rate Line
::

SUBSECTION:: Wrapping

link::#-wrap:: derives a new UDef that pre-binds the original's function as a
code::func:: argument of a wrapper. This lets you build variations that inject the
base graph into a surrounding network. The wrapper function must take a code::func::
argument; the original UDef's function of the same rate is bound to it.

code::
UDef(\osc, ar: { |freq = 440| SinOsc.ar(freq) });

// a wrapper that runs the base graph through a filter
UDef(\osc).wrap(\filtered, ar: { |func, cutoff = 800|
    LPF.ar(func.value, cutoff)
});

UDef('osc.filtered').ar(freq: 220, cutoff: 400);
::

CLASSMETHODS::

METHOD:: new
Fetch or create the UDef registered under code::name::. If code::ar::, code::kr::,
or code::ir:: functions are supplied they are stored (see link::#-set::).

ARGUMENT:: name
A link::Classes/Symbol:: identifying the UDef.

ARGUMENT:: ar
A link::Classes/Function:: defining the audio-rate graph.

ARGUMENT:: kr
A link::Classes/Function:: defining the control-rate graph.

ARGUMENT:: ir
A link::Classes/Function:: defining the scalar/initialization-rate graph.

returns:: The registered UDef instance.

INSTANCEMETHODS::

METHOD:: ar
Evaluate the audio-rate function, splicing its UGen graph into the enclosing
SynthDef. Arguments (positional or keyword) are forwarded to the function.

METHOD:: kr
As link::#-ar::, for the control-rate function.

METHOD:: ir
As link::#-ar::, for the scalar-rate function.

METHOD:: arFunc, krFunc, irFunc
The link::Classes/Function:: defining each rate. Assignable.

METHOD:: arArgs, krArgs, irArgs
An link::Classes/Event:: of the argument names and default values for each rate's
function, or code::nil:: if that rate is undefined.

METHOD:: set
Store the code::ar:: / code::kr:: / code::ir:: functions (only the non-nil ones)
and record the defining file's path. Called automatically by link::#*new::.

METHOD:: wrap
Return a new UDef named code::"name.wrapName":: whose rate functions wrap this
UDef's functions. Each wrapper function receives the original function bound to its
code::func:: argument. See the discussion above.

ARGUMENT:: wrapName
A link::Classes/Symbol:: suffixed to this UDef's name for the derived UDef.

ARGUMENT:: ar
ARGUMENT:: kr
ARGUMENT:: ir
Wrapper functions for each rate. Each must take a code::func:: argument.

METHOD:: multichannelExpand
If code::true::, calling link::#-ar:: / link::#-kr:: / link::#-ir:: with array
arguments performs multichannel expansion across the arguments (like a real UGen).
Defaults to code::false::.

METHOD:: path
The path of the file in which this UDef was last defined.

METHOD:: open
Open the defining file (link::#-path::) in the editor, if known.

EXAMPLES::

See the code::examples/pluck.scd:: file in this quark for a full
Karplus-Strong-style plucked string built as a UDef.
